've  ever seen malice also known as evil  represented tangibly like this and in  this quantity and it's also the first  time we've ever seen ganondorf wielding  or producing any kind of power that  doesn't stem from either his own wizard  abilities or the triforce of power much  less while being you know dead the  question i'd like to ask here is this  even if demise's malicious intent has  existed in some way for the entirety of  the zelda franchise which i'm not  questioning what happened to make it  manifest specifically this way in breath  of the wild what made malice breath of  the wild has long been speculated as  being heavily inspired by the works of  studio ghibli particularly the movie  called princess mononoke i mean fans of  the film will pretty clearly see the  visual resemblances between link and the  film's protagonist ashitaka they're both  youthful boys who dress in tunics and  hoodies wielding bows and arrows and  swords riding through very green fields  on the backs of their trusty steeds they  also both have hearts of gold and epic  combat skills i happen to believe that  malice is also inspired by a substance  we see in princess mononoke spoiler  warning for those who haven't seen the  movie by the way near the end of the  film the humans led by lady aboshi  remove the head of the dear god turning  its body into a corrupted version of the  nightwalker spilling sentient goop all  over the land that removes the life of  anything it comes in contact with this  corrupted dear god goop is what i  believe malice was inspired by as well  both are similarly goopy are sentient  and will destroy life on contact they're  also both of a similar coloration but  there is one more similarity that the  substances share that we weren't able to  see until the breath of the wild 2  trailer and that is the fact that in  either case the goopy substance  originates from an individual in the  film the mononoke malice originates from  the deer god's body and in breath of the  wild malice comes from ganondorf's  corpse but the reason why i'm taking so  long to cover their similarities is to  point out the fact that mononoke malice  wasn't created without something  happening to its point of origin the  deer god and i believe the same could be  true for ganondorf the deer god stimulus  was its head being removed making the  mononoke malice spread but ganondorf  still has his head could something else  have happened to his body that resulted  in the creation of malice well let me  set something up real quick before  answering that in breath of the wild we  can see the minions of ganon everywhere  but their quote-unquote leader calamity  gannon is a mindless monster who is  incapable of speech how could this  amalgamation of weaponry and goop have  possibly intelligently formulated armies  and led forces against hyrule well let  me tell you a story once upon a time the  legend of zelda was a new franchise 35  years ago in fact the first zelda game  was so well received that nintendo made  a sequel and this sequel was called  zelda 2 and because it was a direct  sequel it had to take place after the  events of the original game this was  before the sloppy timeline stuff anyway  so story wise since link defeated ganon  at the end of the first game ganon was  effectively dead in the second game but  yet his minions ran around the world of  hyrule trying to kill link just the same  but why you ask their leader was dead so  they should have just you know given up  right well in the official game manual  we're given some insight into the  reasoning behind ganon's monsters still  roaming about you see they wanted to  kill link so that they could then drain  the blood from his body and sprinkle it  over the ashes of the evil king doing so  according to this official manual would  revive ganon now back to breath of the  wild i'm not trying to say for certain  which timeline the game takes place in  but many people already believe it takes  place at the end of the fallen timeline  matpat from game theory even has a  pretty compelling theory about this  placement as well if this is the case  then that places breath of the wild  immediately after zelda 2 in the  timeline the last thing we knew about  ganon was that he was indeed dead but  his minions were trying to revive him  with the blood of the link that killed  him the link from zelda 1. we can only  assume that the minions were trying to  accomplish what we saw them attempting  to do in zelda 2 and that is to find  link and revive ganon and what we are  left with in the game breath of the wild  is a revived form of ganon created out  of malice by the way have you ever  wondered why malice seems oddly familiar  as a substance i mean it's this weird  dark reddish purplish goop that we've  never seen in a video game before but it  is very similar to a certain real-life  substance that everyone is familiar with  blood malice has many similarities to  coagulated blood such as its goopy  sticky sometimes stringy nature and  deeply red color calamity ganon's  resurrection cocoon in the royal chamber  of hyrule castle is even stylized to  resemble a hanging human heart and has  veins delivering malice to and from the  cocoon much like our blood vessels  deliver blood to and from our hearts the  creations of pure malice the ganons are  all oddly shaped because they have no  actual solid form they're just globs of  coagulated malice with shika technology  scattered throughout their bodies and  they bleed out violently when defeated  the final piece to this blood puzzle  would be the fact that malice has been  shown to originate from ganondorf's  corpse giving even more credence to its  similarities to blood but the final  question remains if malice is a form of  corrupted blood that's coming from  ganondorf's corpse why is his blood so  powerful and infinitely limitless well  what if it's not just his blood but the  corrupted blood of link from zelda 2. if  you think about it the only way to  ensure that link's blood from zelda 2  wouldn't be used for the revival of  ganon would be to hide link's body away  after he dies of his eventual natural  death given that link was able to even  avoid being killed and captured by  ganon's minions for his entire life in  the first place however keeping  something like that hidden would be  impossibly difficult especially when you  take into consideration the limitless  amount of time that ganon's minions have  to roam about searching for the body so  what if they eventually were successful  and did in fact pour link's blood onto  the corpse of ganondorf after the events  of zelda 2 corrupting it with demise's  malicious hatred that resided within  ganondorf and turning it into malice  with the sole purpose of reviving ganon  that would explain why even though  malice is an obviously supernatural  substance that spreads infinitely and  can even corrupt pools of water in  hyrule to spread further it ultimately  serves to form ganons over and over  again and at certain intervals on  certain nights ganon's malice surges in  power across the land of hyrule under  the light of a blood moon so there you  have it my crazy short theory that  malice could actually be the tainted  blood of the hero now how does the green  hand from the trailer tie into all this  i'm not sure to be honest while it does  appear to be some sort of either living  or man-made construct that's attempting  to stop the outward flow of malice from  ganondorf's corpse it also seems to be  not only kind of failing at that job but  also extracting the malice from the body  as nintendo black crisis discovered in a  video last year some people speculate  that it's the soul of a previous link  and with this theory that could imply  that it is the soul of link from zelda 2  trying to do something to prevent the  spread of malice but i digress it's just  too vague to figure out for sure at this  point once again this theory is